# Drawing Rectangles on Canvas 🖌️

To draw on a canvas, grab its 2D rendering context with `.getContext('2d')`:

```html_not
<canvas id="rectCanvas" width="300" height="150"></canvas>

<script>
  const canvas = document.getElementById('rectCanvas');
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  // Set fill color
  ctx.fillStyle = '#3b82f6';
  // fillRect(x, y, width, height)
  ctx.fillRect(20, 20, 150, 80);

  // Stroked outline rectangle
  ctx.strokeStyle = '#ef4444';
  ctx.lineWidth = 4;
  ctx.strokeRect(100, 50, 150, 80);
</script>
```

# Canvas Paths, Lines, and Circles ⭕

For custom shapes, lines, and arcs, use path methods:

```html_not
<canvas id="pathCanvas" width="300" height="200"></canvas>

<script>
  const ctx = document.getElementById('pathCanvas').getContext('2d');

  // 1. Draw a Line
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.moveTo(30, 30);   // Starting coordinate
  ctx.lineTo(200, 30);  // Ending coordinate
  ctx.strokeStyle = '#10b981';
  ctx.lineWidth = 3;
  ctx.stroke();

  // 2. Draw a Circle: arc(x, y, radius, startAngle, endAngle)
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.arc(150, 120, 40, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
  ctx.fillStyle = '#f59e0b';
  ctx.fill();
  ctx.stroke();
</script>
```

# Drawing Text on Canvas ✍️

You can render formatted typography directly onto the canvas bitmap:

```html_not
<canvas id="textCanvas" width="400" height="100"></canvas>

<script>
  const ctx = document.getElementById('textCanvas').getContext('2d');

  ctx.font = '24px Inter, sans-serif';
  ctx.fillStyle = '#1e293b';
  ctx.fillText('Canvas 2D Typography', 20, 50);

  // Outlined text
  ctx.font = 'bold 30px Arial';
  ctx.strokeStyle = '#6366f1';
  ctx.strokeText('Outlined Text', 20, 90);
</script>
```

Text drawn on canvas is rasterized pixels—it cannot be highlighted or selected with a cursor like standard HTML text!
